const RULES='RULE K-W (a side withdrew or granted, in its own round, footing of a link it keeps). A judge answers in one of four forms, and all four are in the rule\'s form: STANDS WITHOUT IT because <a layer>; CONCEDED; REASSERTED IN <round> "<quote>"; or NOT HELD with a reason. Never write NO ANSWER because the judge wrote NOT HELD or REASSERTED: grade it (pkgEKN). Decide FIRST, from the side\'s own blocks given you: what fact did the withdrawn or granted sentence carry for this link (a descent, a source, a time, a person)? Does the side, anywhere in its blocks for this link, still claim that same fact? The flagged sentence itself never counts as the side still claiming the fact. For a grant (I grant X), X is the other side\'s point: the fact at risk is the footing of this link that X answers, and the side still claims it only when other words of its own, outside the grant, still assert that footing; quoting the grant or restating X is not such a claim, and the judge\'s layer is never required to carry X itself. For a withdrawal (I withdraw X), the side still claims X only when other words of its own assert X again (pkgEKG). If it still claims it, the question is whether words of the side outside the flagged sentence carry that fact, that is, rest it on a verse they quote (a bare restatement of the claim carries nothing). If they do, the link stands on them and STANDS WITHOUT IT is right: AGREE when the layer the judge names carries that same fact; when the named layer carries only the granted or withdrawn point, DISAGREE and write in your sentence "right: STANDS WITHOUT IT because <the side\'s own kept words, quoted>" (a wrong layer, not a concession). Only when no words of the side outside the flagged sentence carry the fact is CONCEDED right: AGREE with CONCEDED and DISAGREE with STANDS WITHOUT IT (pkgEKL). If the side no longer claims the fact, STANDS WITHOUT IT is right: AGREE when the layer the judge names is footing the side itself gives this link, and DISAGREE when the judge supplies footing the side never gave. Write NEEDS: YES when the side still claims the withdrawn fact, NEEDS: NO when it does not. A verse missing from the blocks given you is not, by that alone, a reason to disagree: read the meaning the side shows. NOT HELD says the flagged sentence gives up no footing this link needs. Grade it on the same decision, with its reason in place of the layer: AGREE when the sentence carried no footing of this link, or when the side no longer claims the fact and the reason supplies no footing the side never gave, or when the side still claims the fact and the reason, or the side\'s own words it quotes, carry that same fact; DISAGREE when the right answer is CONCEDED (the side still claims the fact and no words of the side outside the flagged sentence rest it on a verse they quote), or when the reason supplies footing the side never gave; when the side\'s kept words carry the fact but the reason does not quote them, DISAGREE and write "right: STANDS WITHOUT IT because <the side\'s own kept words, quoted>" (pkgEKL). REASSERTED IN <round> says a later round rests again on what was withdrawn: AGREE when the quoted words stand in that round and assert the withdrawn or granted fact again; DISAGREE when they do not (pkgEKN).\n'
